= Decision theory — Technical =

For a finite set of outcomes, a common expected-utility form is <pre>EU(a) = Σ_s P(s|a) U(a,s)</pre>where an action a is evaluated across possible states s. Representation theorems state conditions under which preference orderings can be represented by utility functions. Different theories disagree about which probabilities, causal dependencies, preference axioms, or decision rules are appropriate.

== Modeling cautions ==
* decision theory ≠ psychology of choice by definition
* decision theory ≠ expected-utility theory only
* formal optimality ≠ factual or moral correctness

